{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CL4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0002": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{Z}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-image-proper-is-proper}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:902b9920347a9466863cb0de6dcaf44bef115416116307aff18b8af91558f715", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c9f4bd69f9785ed11936fe2e4318d601f0cfd3502bd1d6e134ca5ca49691c1e3", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack.\nLet <MATH_0002>\nbe a morphism of algebraic stacks over <MATH_0003>.\nIf <MATH_0004> is universally closed over <MATH_0005>\nand <MATH_0006> is surjective then <MATH_0007>\nis universally closed over <MATH_0008>.\nIn particular, if also <MATH_0009> is\nseparated and of finite type over <MATH_0010>,\nthen <MATH_0011> is proper over <MATH_0012>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:416e5e94fefe6e605aabdcba4b1759c8a3e77e970c7c013a06e62758c9185c49", "unit_id": "tag:0CQK:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0CL4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$p : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$q : \\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{Z}' \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0006": "$f' : \\mathcal{X}' \\to \\mathcal{Y}'$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{Z}' \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0009": "$p' : \\mathcal{X}' \\to \\mathcal{Z}'$", "MATH_0010": "$p$", "MATH_0011": "$T \\subset |\\mathcal{Y}'|$", "MATH_0012": "$(f')^{-1}(T) \\subset |\\mathcal{X}'|$", "MATH_0013": "$p'((f')^{-1}(T)) = q'(T)$", "MATH_0014": "$q'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-lemma-base-change-surjective}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e4e42081e9b9b1df04b3deaa69b3e54156e22beffec29cc689e7b02bf350ad48", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:36d9c895207689d0ac8ef56f7f2315db1de5ef21366a4774fff409b115faaac1", "source_text": "Assume <MATH_0001> is universally closed and <MATH_0002> surjective.\nDenote <MATH_0003>,\n<MATH_0004> the structure morphisms.\nLet <MATH_0005> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nThe base change <MATH_0006>\nof <MATH_0007> by <MATH_0008> is surjective\n(Properties of Stacks, Lemma\n<REF_0001>) and the base\nchange <MATH_0009> of <MATH_0010> is closed.\nIf <MATH_0011> is closed, then\n<MATH_0012> is closed, hence\n<MATH_0013> is closed. So <MATH_0014> is closed.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9c184300accb99482b54163073d67396bb10848f153897bc16e8f4e8b096cf44", "unit_id": "tag:0CQK:proof"}
